{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793010532,"nonce":"L+Y5uQeLqh6woVa6YIoeQlfyDKo=","title":"Run browser terminals through session PTYs without native cterm calls","message":"Reproduced the reported crash in the staged browser app by opening Terminal: RayDE stops with Native library cterm not loaded / term_open_background. The browser also discovers profiles through its mounted workspace filesystem instead of the remote host.\n\nSplit the existing native PTY/screen engine from HashLink FFI and reuse the pure engine in the Rust session. Add authenticated connection-owned bounded PTYs, nonblocking startup/input/resize/scroll/close, coalesced acknowledged screen patches, hidden-view suspension and disconnect cleanup. Browser terminal methods read a bounded local screen mirror, and async operations use ash-future/session RPC. Ship safe unavailable/readiness/error states when a demo or no-exec session has no terminal; no WASM code path may call cterm. Discover shell profiles on the session host. Preserve Unicode selection, ANSI, alternate screen and PTY dimensions.\n\nVerify real browser terminal opening, input/output, resize, ANSI, multiple terminals, hide/reopen and session loss without app failure. Native tests cover PTY status, ownership/auth/limits, output backpressure, process cleanup and FFI compatibility. Rebuild WASM and session, stage/restart the existing endpoint for user testing.\n\nRelated browser follow-ups: 6b1af5b5288a9992eb38813eda814cf769f17ed0c6d4bfc98f39c38c9d300c83. Broader PTY/provider/isolation track 670bd15d5f2a4c8fdd82da62e9b72599f9a689affc5682a7b621f81fd72156c0 remains open for MSB/provider rollout.","files":null}]}